  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "Admission checks and gateway requests",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "description": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Guard admission checks cover public API and Grafana traffic before authentication.** They count requests reaching the admission handler; earlier connection, header and handler-cap rejections are excluded. Inference counters cover real public inference attempts, not synthetic probes or successful completions. **Caddy charts select the measured top-level public route (`handler=\"subroute\"`)** and combine API and Grafana requests, including authentication failures and guard rejections. Durations measure server handling through that route, including authentication, upstream work and streamed responses. They are not client end-to-end latency or LLM-only response time. Private metrics listeners are excluded."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Caddy exporter",
      "type": "stat",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "description": "",
